course: dictionary
lesson: 732
title: Basic: simple, plain, and essential
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Basic has a few jobs. It can mean simple and most important, the first part everything else is built on, like «basic facts» and «basic skills». You learn the basics before you try hard problems.
explain: Basic can also mean plain, with no extras. «A basic version of a product has fewer features.» So a basic phone can call and text, but it has no fancy camera or games. Read the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: Basic needs are things everyone must have to live: food, water, shelter and safety. The context helps here: «The cost of living is how much money people need for basic things» tells you basic means essential, not plain.
explain: You can also use basic as a noun in «the basics», meaning the simplest, most important parts of something. Check your meaning by swapping it in: «knowing the basics yourself helps you check it» still makes sense if basics means the important, simple parts you already know.
fact: Basic means simple and most important, the first part that everything else is built on.
fact: Basic also means plain, without extras, like «a basic room».
fact: Basic needs are things everyone must have to live: food, water, shelter and safety.
fact: «The basics» means the simplest, most important parts of a subject or skill.
fact: In chemistry, basic means alkaline, the opposite of acidic.
exercise: In maths, which of these is a basic fact? | Why the sky is blue | A long word problem about trains | A question nobody has answered yet | *3 x 4 = 12
exercise: «A basic phone» can call and text but has no fancy extras. What does basic mean? | *Plain, with no extras | Very expensive | Able to play music loudly | Made of gold
exercise: Lily says basic needs means toys and games. What is the right meaning? | Things you only use on Sundays | *Food, water, shelter and safety, things everyone must have to live | Toys and games | Things that cost a lot of money
test: What does «back to basics» most likely mean? | Playing a new game | Buying the newest model | Forgetting everything you have learned | *Going back to the simplest, most important things
test: «The United States Constitution is the set of basic rules for how a country is run.» Basic here means: | Very old and broken | Silent and secret | Plain and ugly | *Most important, the foundation
exam: Which meaning does basic have in «a basic version of a product has fewer features»? | *Plain, with fewer extras | Simple and most important | Very hungry | Alkaline, like soap
